                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Serious Sam HD: The First Encounter, a remake of the first game to carry the Serious Sam name. It doesn't look bad and plays alright, but it is quite short. There is only one campaign to play through here and several of the earlier levels are pretty much just speedbumps that you play through. \n\nTo describe the gameplay though, expect fairly linear maps that you walk through, with fairly simple objectives to complete to progress through. The enemy composition is slightly meager here - you have several foes that simple just run up to you or try to run through you, then some that attack at range. In later stages you get higher concentrations of enemies attacking you, with the final level having 'lots' attacking you. The end boss is 'not' fun to fight, requiring you to jump through hoops (literally) to beat him.\n\nIf you get this on steep discount then it is certainly worth it to see where the series started, but I would stay away otherwise.",
